[
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-01",
    "role": "opening",
    "config": {
      "text": "Don't open the box.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Pandora's box is one of the best-known images from Greek myth.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "A woman is given a box, she is told never to open it, and when she does, every evil in the world escapes.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "But in the oldest source we have, there is no box.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "And the story it tells is stranger than the one we remember.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P02-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In this episode, we follow Pandora from a Greek poet of around 700 BCE, through ancient storage jars and a later fable, to a Renaissance scholar's book of proverbs and the paintings that gave her the box we know today.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P03-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The earliest account comes from Hesiod, the same poet who described the birth of Medusa.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P03-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In two of his poems, the Theogony and the Works and Days, Pandora's story begins with fire.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P03-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Prometheus has stolen fire from Zeus and given it to humans.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P03-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Zeus answers with a gift of his own.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P04-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "At his command, the smith god Hephaestus shapes a young woman from earth and water.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P04-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Athena teaches her weaving and dresses her.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P04-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Aphrodite gives her grace, and painful longing.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P04-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "And Hermes gives her, in Hesiod's words, a shameless mind and a deceitful nature.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P04-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Because all who lived on Olympus gave her a gift, she is named Pandora, the \"all-gifted.\"",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P05-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In the Theogony, she is not even named.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P05-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Hesiod calls her a beautiful evil, a trap set for humankind, and presents her as the first of all women.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P05-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "His poems are openly hostile to women.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P05-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "That view belongs to Hesiod and his time, and it is one more reason to read the source carefully.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P06-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In the Works and Days, Hesiod tells what happened next.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P06-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Prometheus had warned his brother Epimetheus never to accept a gift from Zeus.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P06-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "But Epimetheus accepted her.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P06-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Before this, people had lived free from evils, from hard work, and from sickness.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P06-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Then she lifted the great lid of a jar and scattered what was inside.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P06-06",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Countless troubles spread among humankind.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P07-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The Greek word Hesiod uses is pithos, a large storage jar for grain, oil, or wine.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P07-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "This one, made on Crete around 675 BCE and now in the Louvre, is about one and a half meters tall.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P07-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Hesiod does not say where the jar came from.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P07-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "And the only warning in his poem is about accepting the gift, not about opening the jar.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P08-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Only one thing stayed inside.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P08-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Hope remained beneath the rim of the jar.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P08-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Before it could fly out, the lid stopped it, by the will of Zeus.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P09-01",
    "role": "question",
    "config": {
      "text": "Why hope?",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P09-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Readers have argued about this line for centuries.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P09-03",
    "role": "question",
    "config": {
      "text": "Is hope kept safe for us, or kept away from us?",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P09-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The Greek word, elpis, can mean hope, but also expectation of what is to come.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P09-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Hesiod does not explain.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P10-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Greek artists also told the story of Pandora's making.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P10-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The ancient traveler Pausanias wrote that her birth was shown in relief on the base of the great statue of Athena inside the Parthenon.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P10-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The statue itself is lost.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P10-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "But this small copy from Roman times still carries a version of that scene on its base.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "And the jar did not always hold evils.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "A later Greek fable, collected under the name of Babrius, tells of a jar that Zeus filled with good things.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "A man who could not resist lifted the lid, and the good things flew up to the heavens.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Only hope was left behind.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In this fable, Pandora is not even named.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-01",
    "role": "question",
    "config": {
      "text": "So where did the box come from?",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The change is usually traced to the early 1500s, more than two thousand years after Hesiod.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The Dutch scholar Erasmus retold the story in Latin, in his famous collection of proverbs, the Adages.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In this edition, printed in Venice in 1508, where Hesiod had pithos, a great jar, Erasmus wrote pyxis, a small box.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "And in his retelling, it is Epimetheus, not Pandora, who opens it.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P13-01",
    "role": "question",
    "config": {
      "text": "Why a box?",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P13-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Scholars have suggested that Erasmus may have been thinking of another story, the Roman tale of Psyche.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P13-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "She is sent to the underworld to bring back a small box, and is warned not to look inside.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P13-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "On the way back, she opens it.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P13-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Whatever the reason, the word stuck.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P14-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Erasmus's book was read across Europe.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P14-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Later artists gave Pandora many kinds of containers: caskets, chests, and vessels.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P14-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Some still showed a great jar, like this print from the 1500s.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P14-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "But over time, the box became the familiar image, and \"Pandora's box\" became an everyday phrase in English, for something that brings many troubles once it is opened.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P15-01",
    "role": "question",
    "config": {
      "text": "So was Pandora's box ever a box?",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P15-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In Hesiod, it is a great storage jar.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P15-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In a later fable, the jar holds good things.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P15-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In a Renaissance book of proverbs, it becomes a small box.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P15-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "And in paintings, it is whatever the artist imagined.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P16-01",
    "role": "conclusion",
    "config": {
      "text": "The box we know is not the oldest part of the story.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P16-02",
    "role": "conclusion",
    "config": {
      "text": "It is one of the newest.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P16-03",
    "role": "conclusion",
    "config": {
      "text": "Every story has an origin.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
